{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/108125-vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-mods","id":108125,"title":"Vampire: the Masquerade Bloodlines mods","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-08T05:30:52-07:00","id":108125,"title":"Vampire: the Masquerade Bloodlines mods","content":"I recently decided to give this game another shot. It's been lying in my Steam library for quite a while. With that in mind, any mods you folks can recommend? I installed the Unofficial Patch, but there may be more. Are the mods with clan-based content good? I think I also wouldn't mind a mod with some new outfits because damn, the way the Nosferatu dress in this game is ridiculous. They wouldn't be quite as much of a walking Masquerade breach if they wore a hoodie that's one size too big, instead of... gimp gear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T19:48:08-07:00","id":108868,"title":"","content":"Not that I've found, but I'm happy the unofficial mod restored a few options that were cut/disabled from the retail release. Playing an Anda Gangrel for my first playthrough, I have to go back and pick up the game again sometime, between Christmas and now I've built up a glut of games that I haven't had time to play. Titanfall has been eating up quite a bit of my gaming time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T20:56:36-07:00","id":108924,"title":"","content":"I wish I knew of some good ones, but I agree that some of the armor choices in the game were.... odd. The Malkavian one in particular stands out to me.<br /> <br /> Actually the Malkavian in general stands out to me, and I think they did an excellent job at walking the fine line between showing just how damaged you really were, and unplayability as you had to guess a lot in dialogue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T03:47:27-07:00","id":109150,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Malkavian outfits are just... bonkers. But at least Malkavians really are mentally disturbed, and their weird outfits aren't Masquerade breaches. I'm still wondering if I feel like playing a Nosferatu throughout the whole game. It's interesting that you need to do a lot of things differently, but it also gets a bit annoying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T09:33:06-07:00","id":109371,"title":"","content":"I know the Malks were adored by many, but I found them a little high on the &quot;insane is fun rather than scary&quot; spectrum. The Camarilla and Final Nights mods are excellent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T10:19:00-07:00","id":109399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/108125-vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-mods?p=109150#post109150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the Malkavian outfits are just... bonkers. But at least Malkavians really are mentally disturbed, and their weird outfits aren't Masquerade breaches. I'm still wondering if I feel like playing a Nosferatu throughout the whole game. It's interesting that you need to do a lot of things differently, but it also gets a bit annoying.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should try it, definitely. Nosferatu get excellent starting bonuses, and IMO Obfuscate is one of the most useful Disciplines in the game. The game acts like you'll have to strain yourself to avoid detection, but as long as you don't get right up in anyone's face, you won't trigger a Masquerade breach. And if that wasn't enough, Nosferatu get more special dialogue than usual, and get to bypass some social checks. It's awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T14:19:34-07:00","id":109619,"title":"","content":"Getting three Vitae from rats is highly useful, certainly. It makes feeding a lot easier, since you can just hop into the sewer and munch on a couple, instead of hunting for humans. And yeah, you can slink around without being detected quite easily.<br /> <br /> Oh, and another thing - does anyone know what you need to figure out that Knox is just playing stupid? I think I've heard about it being possible, but I don't know how.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T19:19:04-07:00","id":109773,"title":"","content":"I can't remember where I found it but I have a reskin for the nos that takes off the gimp mask at least. And the clan quests are ok. Only part I really liked was it tells you more about the kuei jin.<br /> You could try the companion mod. It runs an older version of the unofficial patch but its worth it. <a href=\"http://www.moddb.com/mods/vtmb-companion-mod\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.moddb.com/mods/vtmb-companion-mod</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1303-zap-rowsdower","name":"zap rowsdower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T19:21:52-07:00","id":109775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/108125-vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-mods?p=109619#post109619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and another thing - does anyone know what you need to figure out that Knox is just playing stupid? I think I've heard about it being possible, but I don't know how.</div> </div> </div> </div> 4 dots in perception I think. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1303-zap-rowsdower","name":"zap rowsdower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T03:53:53-07:00","id":109996,"title":"","content":"Looks like I won't be doing that with my Nosferatu... shame. I really wanted to see how it looks like. As far as a companion mod goes, I generally avoid NPC helpers in such games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}